---
import CaptureModule from '../CaptureModule.astro';

/**
 * The index's panel around the site's one capture module.
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. This is chrome and copy: the raised panel
 * the index canvas draws, the kicker, the heading and the one paragraph saying
 * what the digest is. It asks for nothing. Everything that asks for an address,
 * and every statement about what happens to one, is CaptureModule, which every
 * capture surface on the site composes.
 *
 * WHY IT REPLACED A SECOND MODULE. Until 2026-08-17 this file was
 * `EmailCapture.astro` and it was a whole second capture module: its own
 * endpoint constant, its own form, its own honest state, its own mail link. The
 * Desk composed the other one. Two modules asking for an address is two promises
 * about what happens to it, and the two were not even agreeing: this one shipped
 * an announcement because it had nowhere to post, while the other shipped a live
 * POST to a path a static build never emits, so a submit on /desk was a 404. One
 * module now answers the question, and the panel is the only thing that differs
 * between the surfaces, because the panel is the only thing that should.
 *
 * The name changed with the job. A file called EmailCapture that captures
 * nothing is a file whose name has to be read twice.
 */
---

<section class="digest" aria-labelledby="digest-title">
  <p class="kicker digest-kicker">The weekly digest</p>
  <h2 class="digest-title" id="digest-title">One email a week, and nothing else</h2>

  <p class="digest-detail">
    The roles that arrived since the last one, the postings that died in between, and one number
    from the sweep. No feed to scroll, no re-sends, and your address goes nowhere else.
  </p>

  {/*
    watchFilters, because this page is the one that renders Filters. The alerts
    consent reads the table's filter state and names it back, so the consent says
    what it stores. It is inert until there is a list, and so is everything else
    in the module, which is the point of composing it rather than copying it.
  */}
  <CaptureModule source="index" watchFilters class="digest-capture" />
</section>

<style>
  .digest {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-300);
    padding: var(--space-600);
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-line-strong);
  }

  .digest-kicker {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* The section heading role, one step down from the page title, set by
     global.css on h2. Only the measure is this module's business. */
  .digest-title {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .digest-detail {
    font-size: var(--size-200);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    max-width: var(--layout-measure);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* The panel already set the gap between its own blocks. The module keeps its
     own internal rhythm and only needs the step above it, so nothing here
     reaches inside a component this file does not own. */
  .digest-capture {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-200);
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) { /* --breakpoint-phone */
    .digest {
      padding: var(--space-500) var(--space-400);
    }
  }
</style>
